      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["D9", "D10"],
      "pins": ["D10.1", "D10.2", "D10.3", "D10.4", "D9.1", "D9.2", "D9.3", "D9.4", "U11.6", "U11.7", "U10.6", "U10.7"],
      "nets": ["CAN0_P", "CAN0_N", "CAN1_P", "CAN1_N", "CANH", "CANL"],
      "observed": "On the CAN BUS sheet, the references D9 and D10 are drawn as dual optocouplers (a box with 'Input'/'Output' pins, an internal LED/phototransistor pair and a GND pin) inserted in series between the isolated CAN transceivers U11/U10 (CANH/CANL) and the CAN0/CAN1 differential pair nets (CAN0_P/CAN0_N, CAN1_P/CAN1_N). No CDSOT23-SM712 TVS array symbol appears anywhere on the CAN buses.",
      "expected": "The specification states D9 and D10 are CDSOT23-SM712 TVS diode arrays placed on CAN0_P/N and CAN1_P/N for CAN bus transient/ESD protection, and that the CAN isolation is provided by the isolated transceiver U11 (and its CAN1 companion) — not by optocouplers in the bus lines. The reference netlist's CDSOT23-SM712 at D9/D10 'matches this documented choice'.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "CAN BUS sheet: 'D10' box with pins 'Input 2 / Input 1 / Output 3 / Output / GND' wired between U11 CANH/CANL and the CAN0_P / CAN0_N nets; 'D9' drawn identically on the CAN1 path (U10 CANH/CANL -> D9 -> CAN1_P/CAN1_N)."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "D9, D10 — CDSOT23-SM712 TVS diode arrays on CAN0_P/N, CAN1_P/N | CAN bus transient/ESD protection | ... the netlist's CDSOT23-SM712 matches this documented choice."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (U8, U9) through an isolated CAN transceiver (U11/companion)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The intended SM712 transient/ESD protection on both CAN buses is absent, leaving the M12 CAN connectors (J2/J13) and the Odrive motor controllers exposed to surges/ESD. Worse, the optocouplers are placed in series with the differential pair after the already-isolated transceiver; their open-collector outputs cannot drive the 120-ohm terminated CAN physical layer, so CAN0/CAN1 signaling is broken and the rover cannot communicate with its motor controllers.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The CAN buses deviate from the intended design: where the spec (and the reference netlist) call for CDSOT23-SM712 TVS diode arrays at D9/D10 on CAN0_P/N and CAN1_P/N, this build instead places dual optocouplers in series with the differential lines after the isolated transceivers U11/U10, removing ESD protection and crippling the CAN physical layer. Other flagged items (16 MHz crystals, LTC4412+P-FET, SN74LVC1G07 e-stop buffers, GLOBAL_EN direct switch, PoE jumper) match the documented reference/known issues and are not reported."
}

